e following rivers in\nColorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa County.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Alamosa...Minor flooding\nis forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande  at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From late tonight to late Monday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Minor flooding. Minor agricultural flooding\nin low lying areas along the river\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:30 AM MDT Sunday the stage was 6.8 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage just\nafter midnight tonight to a crest of 9.2 feet tomorrow morning.\nIt will then fall below flood stage tomorrow afternoon.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 9.3\nfeet on 05/18/1944.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-27T03:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8186a07214c5ea0d5bf3b635c9b9fc3f3c6dfd68.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.8186a07214c5ea0d5bf3b635c9b9fc3f3c6dfd68.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 24 at 5:29PM MDT until October 25 at 9:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding likely along the Rio Grande between Monte Vista and\nAlamosa.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Rio Grande County and West Central Alamosa\nCounty...\n\n* WHEN...Until 945 PM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the Rio Grande and low lying agricultural\nareas in Rio Grande and Alamosa counties is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 525 PM MDT, Emergency management reports flooding of low lying\nareas along and near the Rio Grande in Rio Grande county and in\nAlamosa county upstream of the city of Alamosa.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande and West Central\nAlamosa Counties between Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weat